  "result": "Here's a first draft (about 90 words). I haven't added it to `README.md`.\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nCarrier rate cards live in `shop/carriers/`, one module per carrier (20 in total, `acme` through `tundra`). Each module defines a `BASE_RATE` in cents, plus a per-weight rate and a zone multiplier table. `rate(weight, zone)` returns the quote in cents: `(BASE_RATE + per-weight rate \u00d7 weight) \u00d7 zone factor`. Look carriers up by name with `shop.carriers.get(\"acme\")`; the full list is in `REGISTRY` in `shop/carriers/__init__.py`.\n\nEvery carrier takes weight in kilograms except **Maple** (`maple.py`). Maple takes weight in grams (`PER_GRAMS`, max 30,000 g). Convert the weight before you call it.\n```\n\nI checked it against the code. All 20 modules set `BASE_RATE` (for example, Acme 450 and Maple 494). The other 19 use `PER_KG`; only `maple.py` uses `PER_GRAMS` and `MAX_GRAMS`, and its docstring says \"weight in grams.\"\n\nShould I add it to `README.md` below the test command?",
